libspng's own CMakeLists.txt decides whether to link libm by checking CMAKE_HOST_WIN32 -
the OS actually running CMake - rather than WIN32, which reflects the *target* platform
(honors CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME). The two only diverge when cross-compiling, which is exactly what
cmake/xwin-toolchain.cmake does: building from a Linux host for a Windows target, where
CMAKE_HOST_WIN32 is (correctly) false, so libspng always added libm - and since the resulting
SPNGTargets.cmake bakes in a bare "m" with no full path, lld-link failed with "could not open
'm.lib'" the first time anything actually linked against spng (rimutil, in this repo). A
native Windows build (where host and target agree) is unaffected either way.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@
 include(GNUInstallDirs)
 include(CMakePackageConfigHelpers)
 
-if(NOT CMAKE_HOST_WIN32)
+if(NOT WIN32)
     set(MATH_LIBRARY "m")
 else()
     set(MATH_LIBRARY "")
